{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>After these things.</b> Some of our Sages say (Sanhedrin 89) — after the words of the satan, who was prosecuting and saying: Of every feast that Abraham made, he did not sacrifice before You a single bull or a single ram! He said to him: Did he do anything except for the sake of his son? If I were to say to him, 'Slaughter him before Me,' he would not refuse. And some say — after the words of Ishmael, who was boasting over Isaac that he was circumcised at thirteen years and did not protest. Isaac said to him: With one limb you frighten me? If the Holy One, blessed be He, said to me, 'Slaughter yourself before Me,' I would not refuse." "<b>Here I am.</b> So is the answer of the devout — a term of humility and a term of readiness."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:52.308315999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}